Good morning [NAME].

The error you are seeing is related to the [FILE_NAME] perl module. The
module must be configured and compiled for use with [PRODUCT] files.
I'm not sure how to correctly install it when using a debian package
of [PRODUCT]. Using the [PRODUCT] tarball, you would do the
following:

untar the [PRODUCT] tar.gz
cd [FILE_NAME]
cd contrib
tar -zxvf [FILE_NAME]
cd [PRODUCT]-1.051
perl Makefile.PL
make
make install

The [PRODUCT] Makefile will look for the [PRODUCT] files itself. It
expects to find them in the same folder path, so it's important to
follow this exactly as described above.

Let us know how it goes.

Thanks, [NAME]

